frontend-motion adapts and merges two MIT-licensed skills. Their licenses are
kept byte for byte in LICENSE-animate and LICENSE-better-ui.

animate
  By Emil Kowalski, github.com/emilkowalski/skills
  at e8a175de22ae1e49370fc144c1f3bb9aeedf988d
  Used: the build sequence that forms the backbone of SKILL.md (should it
  animate, purpose, tool, properties, easing and duration, interruption and
  exit, reduced motion and pointer gating), the animation recipes in
  references/recipes.md, and part of the "Never ship" table.

better-ui
  By Jakub Krehel, github.com/jakubkrehel/skills
  at d574cc8a576dc24256ad38268b8d03d86724a1b3
  Used: the surface and icon rules with their exact values, the press, enter,
  exit, reduced-motion, theme-switch and performance recipes, the icon and
  surface recipes in references/recipes.md, and part of the "Never ship" table.

Both were read through github.com/23jmo/jmo-skills at 6082bf2c.

Adapted: the two sources are merged into one set of values, and where they
disagreed one value was chosen. Prose was rewritten and shortened, and recipes
were changed to match the chosen values.

Dropped from animate: the rule against presenting motion options, the canned
initial response, the output format, promotional lines, and its links to
companion skills.

Dropped from better-ui: the severity and verdict reporting format, the optical
alignment recipes (one summary rule is kept), agent metadata, and its links to
companion skills.

Where a companion skill carried a rule worth keeping, the rule is stated
directly instead.
